From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Turton <harrisonturton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:21:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Don't check a typed frozen value's type as it's deserialized

A typed value in a cycle, such as a function's module, may be
deserialized before what it points to, whose type can't be read yet.
pagable deserializes the field through the type that serialized it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/values/layout/typed.rs | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/values/layout/typed.rs b/src/values/layout/typed.rs
index 8f43a3e0..41bb7431 100644
--- a/src/values/layout/typed.rs
+++ b/src/values/layout/typed.rs
@@ -475,9 +475,11 @@ impl<'v, T: StarlarkValue<'v>> crate::pagable::StarlarkDeserialize for FrozenVal
         ctx: &mut dyn crate::pagable::starlark_deserialize::StarlarkDeserializeContext<'_>,
     ) -> crate::Result<Self> {
         let fv = FrozenValue::starlark_deserialize(ctx)?;
-        // SAFETY: pagable deserializes this field through the same Rust type
-        // that serialized it.
-        Ok(unsafe { FrozenValueTyped::new_unchecked(fv) })
+        // Pagable deserializes this field through the same Rust type that
+        // serialized it. The value may not be deserialized yet, when values
+        // refer to each other in a cycle, such as a module and the functions
+        // defined in it, so its type isn't checked here.
+        Ok(FrozenValueTyped(fv, marker::PhantomData))
     }
 }
 
